Z||000029||Eric||03-13-2001||11:15 PM||||In my youth, I remember there being a White Castle stand at the Ohio State fair (10-12 years ago).  I made up a game where I would buy two castles every hour on the hour.  I would chuck em down in like a minute and follow the already decaying bolus with a root beer soda.  I would let the stomach settle for a minute, then I would run to the midway enroute to the Octopus (or whatever the most pukestained ride of the day was) and I would ride it till it was time for the second batch of castles.  Once you work through the initial pains, it's easy to go for five or six hours.  Sometimes I would mix it up with a ride down that big yellow slided on a potatoe sack.  My friends just didn't see the humor in this feat of endurance. ||||reg||1
Z||000030||filthyscarecrow||03-13-2001||11:51 PM||||nah, mcdonalds is just as bad. i guess kangaroo is an acquired taste. ok, maybe it's not roo, but whatever meat they use, it shouldn't still be sweating after its demise. ya know who makes the best (and very cheap) burgers? hot&now hamburgers. they're like 50 cents each and a sack of 5 double cheeseburgers is like 4.50. i think they use oatmeal as filler, but they taste like 100% beef. mmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm *drooling* too bad we don't have them here in minneapolis/st.paul.<P>------------------<BR>allow me to show you my exhaust pipes...||||reg||1
